From: Matt
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a4xx: set the A430 CP_DEBUG bootstrap chicken bit

OnePlus 2 bring-up: kgsl (adreno_a4xx.c, a4xx_start) sets CP_DEBUG bit 14
on every A4xx that is not an A420, to "disable the speed up of bootstrap on
A430 and its derivatives". Mainline only sets the A420 bit 29, so on A430
the CP runs with the bootstrap speed-up on.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a4xx_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a4xx_gpu.c
@@ -255,7 +255,7 @@
 	gpu_write(gpu, REG_A4XX_UCHE_TRAP_BASE_HI, upper_32_bits(adreno_gpu->uche_trap_base));
 
 	gpu_write(gpu, REG_A4XX_CP_DEBUG, (1 << 25) |
-			(adreno_is_a420(adreno_gpu) ? (1 << 29) : 0));
+			(adreno_is_a420(adreno_gpu) ? (1 << 29) : (1 << 14)));
 
 	/* On A430 enable SP regfile sleep for power savings */
 	/* TODO downstream does this for !420, so maybe applies for 405 too? */
